I do not tick, but I hold time.
Lose me, and history may not rhyme.
What am I?

I hide in smoke, but I am not fire.
I guide, not fight, though I may inspire.
Who am I?

Feathers sharp, eyes of ice,
I fly through trees not once but twice.
I guard the path, I will not yield,
Until your fate is fully sealed.
Who am I?

I wear no crown, I hold no throne,
But through me, greatness may be known.
Though stitched and cloaked, I carry might,
I aim to dim Tunisia's light.
Who am I?

Before I fall, the way is shut.
Answer me, or stay in the rut.
One question, only one key,
What must you do to pass through me?

Ancient but modern, I walk two times.
Past and future, tangled lines.
Born of queens, I now must fight,
To bring my homeland back to light.
Who am I?

No trees grow here, yet I am a forest.
Through fog and root, you face your test.
Step with care, or pay the price.
What am I?

I do not bleed, I do not breathe,
But secrets through my mouth I leave.
I twist and turn with stone and spice,
And hide the truth behind my lies.
What am I?

You cannot touch me, yet I hold shape.
I speak without words, I guide escape.
Golden symbol on chest and head,
I’m not alive, but never dead.
Who am I?

Though I am silent, I change fate.
When turned, I may be too late.
Grains of gold fall through my heart—
Lose me, and worlds fall apart.
What am I?
